        "original_id": "8eee5e01-0f89-54d0-99b7-a439dd988fe0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sangin, Lashkargah, Afghanistan, Sistan Basin\n- Natural features: Helmand River, Helmand River valley\n- Concepts: altitude, watershed, alternative names\n\nFacts:\n- The Helmand River is the longest river in Afghanistan.\n- The Helmand River is the primary watershed for the endorheic Sistan Basin.\n- The Helmand River is also spelled Helmend, Helmund, and Hirmand, and it is also known by Pashto, Persian, Greek, and Latin names.\n- Sangin is located in the valley of the Helmand River at an altitude of 888 meters.\n- Sangin is located 95 kilometers northeast of Lashkargah.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "37a2ec74-014e-544d-afd8-f45615dfe139",
        "text": "Page: Sangin. Sentence: It is located on in the valley of the Helmand River at 888 m altitude, 95 km to the north-east of Lashkargah.\nPage: Helmand River. Sentence: The Helmand River (also spelled \"Helmend, Helmund, Hirmand\"; Pashto/Persian: هیرمند, هلمند \"Hīrmand, Helmand \", Greek: \"Ἐτύμανδρος \" (\"Etýmandros\"), Latin: \"Erymandrus \") is the longest river in Afghanistan and the primary watershed for the endorheic Sistan Basin.",
